#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:3
msgid "Inject packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:5
msgid ""
"Add extra packages into an existing pipx-managed environment with ``pipx "
"inject``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:9
msgid "Inject a package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:11
msgid "Add ``matplotlib`` to the ``ipython`` environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:13
msgid "$ pipx inject ipython matplotlib"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:17
msgid "Inject several at once, from a requirements file, or both:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:19
msgid ""
"$ pipx inject ipython matplotlib pandas\n"
"$ pipx inject ipython -r useful-packages.txt\n"
"$ pipx inject ipython extra-pkg -r more-packages.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:25
msgid "Scripts can request the versioned result envelope from either command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:27
msgid ""
"$ pipx inject ipython matplotlib --output json\n"
"$ pipx uninject ipython matplotlib --output json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:34
msgid "Add an extra to the environment's app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:36
msgid ""
"Name the main package with the extra to add it. pipx installs the extra from "
"the app's recorded source, so an app installed from a wheel, a directory or "
"a URL keeps that source and the extras it already had:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:39
msgid ""
"$ pipx install ./mytool-1.0-py3-none-any.whl\n"
"$ pipx inject mytool 'mytool[feature]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:44
msgid ""
"A spec that changes anything besides the extras, such as a version or a "
"different path or URL, replaces the app and needs ``--force``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:49
msgid "Expose injected apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:51
msgid ""
"Injected packages do not add their entry points to your ``PATH`` by default. "
"Use ``--include-apps`` to expose them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:53
msgid "$ pipx inject ipython black --include-apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:57
msgid ""
"``--include-deps`` exposes apps and manual pages from every dependency. Use "
"``--include-resources-from PACKAGE`` to expose one dependency, repeating it "
"to select more. Both options imply ``--include-apps``. As with ``pipx "
"install``, a package with no app to expose fails the inject and leaves the "
"environment as it was."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:61
msgid ""
"$ pipx inject robotframework-keyta robotframework-browser-batteries --"
"include-resources-from robotframework-browser"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:65
msgid ""
"For exposing apps from an already-installed environment, see :doc:`expose-"
"apps`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:69
msgid "Other flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:71
msgid ""
"``--force`` / ``-f`` reinstalls the package even when it is already injected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:72
msgid ""
"``--editable`` / ``-e`` installs the package in editable (development) mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:73
msgid ""
"``--with-suffix`` gives the injected package's apps the environment's suffix "
"(injecting ``black`` into ``ipython_3.11`` exposes ``black_3.11``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:75
msgid ""
"``--pip-args`` passes extra arguments to `pip <https://pip.pypa.io/>`__ (for "
"example ``--pip-args='--no-cache-dir'``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:76
msgid "``--index-url`` / ``-i`` sets the package index URL for this inject."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:77
msgid ""
"``--system-site-packages`` only prints a warning; the environment keeps the "
"setting ``pipx install`` gave it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:81
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:83
msgid "$ pipx list --include-injected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/inject-packages.rst:87
msgid "The injected packages appear under their host environment."
msgstr ""
